{"id":"bb33b429-9c06-495f-b448-afd5dab9334a","article_key":"doi:10.1038/s41586-026-11206-y","title":"Alzheimer’s disease genetics converges on microglial and neuronal dysregulation","title_zh":"阿尔茨海默病遗传学汇聚于小胶质细胞和神经元失调","doi":"10.1038/s41586-026-11206-y","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-026-11206-y","abstract":"Alzheimer’s disease (AD) is the most common cause of dementia, with global case numbers projected to reach 153 million in 20501. AD is highly heritable, with twin-based heritability estimates of 60–80%2. Although 1,200 causal loci are predicted to exist for AD3, approximately 80 loci have been associated with AD in two recent studies4,5. Low single-nucleotide polymorphism (SNP)-based heritability estimates have prompted the suggestion that little further common-variant risk remains to be found6. Here we analysed data from 109,479 cases, 74,141 proxy cases, 2,131,799 controls and 499,708 proxy controls from diverse ancestries, identifying 118 loci in a multi-ancestry analysis and 9 additional loci in ancestry-specific analyses, 48 of which are new. We identified new AD risk genes, prioritized potential drug targets, and found that genes upregulated in microglia and downregulated in neurons in cases compared with controls were enriched for AD-associated genetic risk. Moreover, we improved polygenic prediction and estimated a SNP heritability of 16%, nearly threefold higher than previous estimates. Together, our findings show that the common-variant contribution to AD has been substantially underestimated, and reveal new molecular and cellular mechanisms as well as specific targets for future drug development research. A multi-ancestry study of Alzheimer’s disease identifies new risk loci and potential drug targets, implicates microglia and neurons, and reveals a larger common-variant contribution than previously estimated.","abstract_zh":"阿尔茨海默病（AD）是最常见的痴呆症，全球病例数预计到2050年将达到1.53亿例1。AD具有高度遗传性，双胞胎研究估计遗传率为60%–80%2。尽管预计AD存在1200个致病位点3，但最近的两项研究仅发现约80个与AD相关的位点4,5。基于单核苷酸多态性（SNP）的低遗传率估计曾提示，剩余可发现的常见变异风险已不多6。在此，我们分析了来自不同血统的109,479例患者、74,141例代理病例、2,131,799例对照和499,708例代理对照的数据，在多血统分析中鉴定出118个位点，在血统特异性分析中鉴定出9个额外位点，其中48个为新发现。我们鉴定出新的AD风险基因，优先筛选了潜在药物靶点，并发现与对照组相比，患者中小胶质细胞上调以及神经元下调的基因富集于AD相关的遗传风险。此外，我们改进了多基因评分预测，并将SNP遗传率估计为16%，几乎是先前估计值的三倍。我们的研究结果表明，常见变异对AD的贡献已被严重低估，并揭示了新的分子和细胞机制以及未来药物开发研究的具体靶点。一项AD的多血统研究鉴定出新的风险位点和潜在药物靶点，提示小胶质细胞和神经元的参与，并揭示比先前估计更大的常见变异贡献。","snippet":"Alzheimer’s disease (AD) is the most common cause of dementia, with global case numbers projected to reach 153 million in 20501. AD is highly heritable, with twin-based heritability estimates of 60–80%2. Although 1,200 causal loci are predicted to exist for AD3, approximately 80 loci have been associated with AD in two recent studies4,5. Low single-nucleotide polymorphism (SNP)-based heritability estimates have prom…","translated_at":"2026-11-22T00:00:12.129656Z","translation_model":"nvidia/nemotron-3.5-super-vl-120b-a12b","source_category":"doi","article_type":"journal-article","volume":null,"issue":null,"published_at":"2026-10-28T00:00:00","acquired_at":"2026-11-21T23:42:03Z","display_date":"2026-11-21T23:42:03Z","display_date_source":"acquired","online_published_at":"2026-10-28T00:00:00","print_published_at":null,"first_author":"Emil Uffelmann","authors_text":"Emil Uffelmann, Douglas P. Wightman, Shahram Bahrami, Alexey A. Shadrin, Vera Fominykh, Takafumi Ojima, Chenyang Jiang, Christian Benner, Elisa Moreno, Adrian I. Campos, Jesper Q. Thomassen, Emmanuel Minois-Genin, Hei Man Wu, G. Bragi Walters, Richard Sherva, Tian Lin, Xuemin Wang, Julien Bryois, Kristi Krebs, Marijn Schipper, Akira Narita, Alessandro Serretti, Anja H. Simonsen, Anna L. van Seumeren, Anne Corbett, Anne-Brita Knapskog, Annette M. Hartmann, Anouk den Braber, Argonde C. van Harten, Arvid Harder, Arvid Rongve, Bengt O. Madsen, Betty M. Tijms, Bitten Aagaard, Bjørn Lichtwarck, Bjørn-Eivind Kirsebom, Byron Creese, Chandra A. Reynolds, Sara Hägg, Ida K. Karlsson, Christian Erikstrup, Christina Mikkelsen, Clive